# cabin_rain_cap: the rain's deck where it sits on the peak (BUILD_PLAN S7,
# 5.8), a step darker than the overcast's: the sky over it slate, its rim
# glacier blue and its body slate, the sky's own, lowered over the summit
# to a ragged foot, all in the deck's own slate (S7b, Lead call 69): it
# draws no ink, so by day and at dusk the cloud ends in its own slate
# (navy at dusk) with no dark strip over the roof, while the blue-hour and
# night tables send slate to ink, so there its foot is the soft dark edge
# S7 drew. On the far layer, at the plate's origin.
